label: Fetch Direct
description: >-
  Query a county's own ArcGIS FeatureServer for one parcel. The host performs
  the HTTP.

  Corresponds to `fetchParcel` in osceola.ts / manistee.ts / roscommon.ts.

  FRICTION (#10, the one you asked about -- chatty effects): this node is fine
  because a single-parcel query is one request. Its sibling
  `fetchParcelsIntersecting` is not, and does not fit at all. See
  fetchParcelPage.node, which I wrote as a deliberately non-conforming file.
effect: http
input: DirectCountyQuery
output: RawParcelFeature
examples:
  - given:
      DirectCountyQuery:
        pin: "10-003-013-20"
        county: "Osceola"
        endpoint: "https://services8.arcgis.com/FmKMwUEmDSC75SQm/arcgis/rest/services/OsceolaCountyParcels_view/FeatureServer/0/query"
    expect:
      RawParcelFeature:
        county: "Osceola"
        sourceTrust: "verified"
        featureJson: '{"properties":{"PIN":"10 003 013 20","OWNER":"SPRAGUE WILLIAM E","UNIT":"MIDDLE BRANCH TOWNSHIP","Shape__Area":163567.8},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-85.3,44.1],[-85.3,44.2],[-85.2,44.2],[-85.3,44.1]]]}}'
